in @facet/metalogue/materialize

# @mirror/realisation — RETIRED (2026-06-10).
#
# The recognitive turn of the @facet/metalogue conversation moved to
# `@facet/metalogue/materialize` per:
#
#   - Recognition #50 (2026-06-10): the form/substance partition.
#     The discriminator's operation is form-on-form (reads
#     `code/X.ast` form; emits a substrate-altitude verdict —
#     both form-side); placing it under @mirror was a path-space
#     mis-coordinate. @io is form/substance's substance side and
#     was correctly ruled out at #47 retraction; the form-side
#     home that subsumes BOTH directions of the metalogue is
#     `@facet/metalogue`.
#
#   - The metalogue-turn-pair recognition (2026-06-10): the
#     @facet/metalogue conversation has two directions — the shim
#     direction (`shim_X(d) -> species_ast`, substrate utters →
#     species emits) at `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`, and the
#     recognitive direction (`classify(d) -> materialised_file`,
#     species utters → substrate recognises) which lives at
#     `shards/code/metalogue/materialize.mirror`. Both directions
#     share the same metalogue session, the same four laws, the
#     same `species_ast` parametric mechanism. The substrate-
#     pull-correct home for both is the same ground.
#
# Carriers + actions moved (with one substrate-pull-correct rename):
#
#   altitude            → partition
#                         (renamed to avoid the path-space
#                         overload; `altitude` names the substrate-
#                         path coordinate, `partition` names the
#                         form/substance binary)
#   realisable_file     → materialised_file
#                         (renamed for substrate-pull-correct
#                         vocabulary at the new altitude; British-
#                         spelled `realisation` noun stays canonical
#                         in prose at the discipline altitude)
#   classify            → classify
#                         (name preserved; signature lifts from
#                         `(f: ref) -> realisable_file` to
#                         `(d: declaration) -> materialised_file`
#                         per the ground's declaration carrier)
#   is_substrate_realisable → is_materialisable
#                            (renamed for symmetry with the new
#                            home; verb-vocabulary refresh)
#   target_altitude     → target_altitude
#                         (name preserved; the "altitude" here is
#                         the SUBSTRATE-PATH coordinate the verdict
#                         targets, not the form/substance partition
#                         — distinct from the carrier rename)
#
# === Consumer migration ===
#
# Consumers that referenced this shard's surface should update:
#
#   @mirror/realisation              → @facet/metalogue/materialize
#   @mirror/realisation.classify     → @facet/metalogue/materialize.classify
#   @mirror/realisation.altitude     → @facet/metalogue/materialize.partition
#   realisable_file                  → materialised_file
#   is_substrate_realisable          → is_materialisable
#
# The cleanup tick removes this file entirely; this one-tick
# deprecation pointer lets consumers update without breakage.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/code-metalogue-surface.md
#                (the @facet/metalogue spec; the recognitive
#                direction lifts to §2.6 at the new home),
#               docs/insights/2026-06-10-bateson-form-behaviour-
#                as-substrates-first-distinction.md
#                (the form/substance partition recognition #50;
#                grounds the move).
# Related shards: code/metalogue/materialize.mirror (the new
#                  home — the ground of the recognitive turn),
#                 code/rust/materialize.mirror (the Rust-altitude
#                  binding at the new home).
